WEBVTT

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:07.290
You guys are still here?

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.620
Go home already.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.350
Wait! Just a little longer.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.190
I'm studying how to play as a flanker.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.570
Have you learned the rules yet?
That comes first.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.340
Gion-kun...

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.690
How about this bit?

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:24.120
It's got some stuff on how a flanker moves.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:25.480
Let me see.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:26.750
Right here.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.610
It's like watching you back in the day.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.260
Huh? What was that... sir?

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.270
You guys have been playing 
since middle school, right?

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.350
No, Sekizan started in high school.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.630
What? Really?

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:50.170
What club were you in during 
middle school, then?

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:52.030
Baseball? Soccer?

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.980
The Going Home Club.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.220
Seriously?

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.320
I'd hate to be part of <i>your</i> Going Home Club.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.450
What did you just say?

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.210
Why did you start playing rugby, then?

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:07.350
Y-Yeah! I'd be really interested 
in hearing that story.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.510
I convinced him to join.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:02.150
That's weird. Jinko's supposed 
to have a rugby team...

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:05.800
<b>Episode 13
Let's Go To Ryogoku Together</b>

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.240
<b>Rugby Team
 Now Recruiting!</b>

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.240
There it is.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.290
<b>Rugby Team
 Now Recruiting!</b>

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:10.250
But it's in tatters.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.130
Oh well. I guess I'll head over 
to the club room.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.490
Sorry. Are you okay?

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.570
I'm fine.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:21.640
What is it?

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:24.810
Hey, are you a first-year, too?

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.150
My name's Hachioji Mutsumi.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.830
Why don't you come play rugby with me?

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:29.800
No, thanks.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:31.680
You're quick to make decisions.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.850
You'd be good at rugby.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:35.270
What's your name?

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.350
Where's this coming from?

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.860
I don't give my name out to strangers.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.860
But I just told you that 
I'm Hachioji Mutsumi.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.930
I have one older sister 
and two younger brothers.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.930
Eldest Daughter
Mami

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.930
Second Son
Megumu

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:46.930
Third Son
Motomu

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:48.960
My favorite food is curry.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.260
Hachioji Family Special 
All-Meat Curry

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.760
Is that enough info?

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.120
Seriously, what's wrong with you?

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.260
I don't need a club.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:56.620
Go ask someone else.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:59.250
Don't be so cold.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.090
I'm not moving until you tell me your name.

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:04.220
You're awfully persistent.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.570
I'm Sekizan. Sekizan Takuya.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.220
Thanks.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.950
Sekizan-kun, huh?

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:17.220
Since you told me your name,
that must mean you're interested in rugby.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.980
Okay! Let's play together.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:23.150
I don't get how your brain works.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.800
<b>Several Days Later</b>

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:33.460
<b>Beware of
Perverts</b>

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.940
What <i>is</i> he doing?

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:33.460
Let's just keep walking.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:36.100
He should be coming this way soon.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:38.690
There he is.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.000
Sekizan-kun!

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.630
Hey, wait...

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.140
Who are you?

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.470
Oh, please.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.020
We talked for a bit the other day.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.380
I'm Hachioji, from the rugby team.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:54.230
What do you want?

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:58.520
Sekizan-kun, you should totally play rugby!

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.020
Because...

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.780
that penetrating gaze...

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.280
those broad shoulders...

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.150
that impressive lower-body muscle...

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:08.830
It's like you were born to play rugby.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:12.460
I've never played or even 
watched rugby before.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.120
I'm telling you, it's fun.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:21.630
Pushing back your opponents in a scrum
or scoring a try feels awesome.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:26.010
Tackling makes you ooze 
adrenaline like crazy!

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:29.760
And friends you sweat with 
are friends for life.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:33.000
Don't you think building friendships through

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.810
contact sports is what a man's sport 
 and being young are all about?

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:37.520
Huh?

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:41.120
Sorry, but I'm not interested in sports.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.400
The upperclassmen will buy you meals...

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.760
My mother's cooking is good enough.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.070
The cheerleaders will love you.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:51.830
Sekizan-sama 
is so hot~

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:51.830
Do you really play sports 
for such base reasons?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:52.530
Bye.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:06:00.010
Oh, right. The stores near the school
support our rugby team.

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.530
They give you stuff for free.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:02.880
Like taiyaki.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.940
Hey, you reacted.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.670
Do you like sweets?

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:08.910
I hate them.

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:11.280
Well, I'll just pretend you don't.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.790
Anyway, you sure do have an impressive build.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:20.640
Since your frame is so big, you'll bulk up
quickly with a little training.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:24.020
With you on the team, 
we'll be a shoo-in to go to Hanazono.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:28.130
Oh, Hanazono is like Koshien for rugby...

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:31.080
How many guys are on a rugby team?

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.620
Huh? Fifteen.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:34.660
That's a lot.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:39.130
But you're the only one trying to recruit me.

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:42.300
The upperclassmen are busy with practice.

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:43.570
Later.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:49.830
He's surprisingly astute.

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:52.680
But I won't give up!

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.560
I thought you didn't like sweets.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.420
I have an unrivaled sweet tooth.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:04.050
Anyway, you were really 
curt back then, Captain.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:07.950
Anyone would act like that if they 
were followed around by a strange man.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:08.990
You're so mean.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:16.330
But there wasn't any reason for you to 
focus your efforts on one guy, was there?

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:19.350
Gion, you don't get it.

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:23.190
You don't know how difficult and 
important it is for the rugby team

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:24.960
to recruit new members.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.970
The rugby teams of schools like Jinko 
that don't get sports recommendations

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:32.060
are mostly made up of newbies.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:36.590
Most people don't even know what rugby is.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:38.540
You were like that, Gion-kun.

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:39.420
Well, yeah...

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:42.580
And, since rugby's played 
with fifteen players,

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:45.530
it's hard to get a good practice session in
when you only have a few members.

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:49.560
But you'll never recruit anyone 
if you reach out to large groups.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:54.260
That's why you have to go after guys 
who you think have what it takes.

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:57.330
You must've really liked the captain.

00:07:57.770 --> 00:07:59.830
I knew he'd be good.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:05.080
I knew the team would be stronger and 
more entertaining if Sekizan joined.

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:08.520
I'm so happy!

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.950
You finally came out here 
to practice passing with me.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:15.340
It's better than having you come to my
classroom every day and cause a commotion.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.530
Admit it. You actually are interested.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:22.460
Why don't you try throwing that ball to me?

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:25.100
How am I supposed to throw it?

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.320
Don't sweat the small stuff.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:28.360
Come on.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.120
Huh? What?

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.620
Wh-What?

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:43.750
Just checking, but is this <i>really</i> 
your first time playing rugby?

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.120
Yeah.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.500
You never played it in PE 
when you were in middle school?

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:48.630
Nope.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.380
You've never seen it on TV?!

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.130
Nope.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.010
You're a genius!

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:55.510
What?

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.760
I could tell just from that pass.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:00.760
I knew I was right about you.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:04.980
Not many people can throw passes 
as clean and accurate as that.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.870
After all, the rugby ball is uniquely shaped.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:09.020
You've got a real feel for it!

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:09.770
It's amazing!

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:14.400
Are you trying to win me over
with compliments?

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:17.950
Even I can tell that I don't 
have any feel for the game.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.600
There you go again.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.020
I bet you always hit home runs
in baseball, didn't you?

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.330
In fact, I bet you only hit home runs.

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:29.910
I couldn't even touch the ball with the bat.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:32.840
B-But I bet you scored 
amazing goals in soccer!

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.000
I played in goal.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.260
But, in basketball, I bet you can dunk!

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:40.660
I was always spraining my fingers.

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:47.640
You're overestimating my abilities.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:54.310
I-In any case, with that body, 
it'd be a crime if you didn't play a sport.

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:59.450
I know my strengths and 
weaknesses better than anyone.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.660
If anything, my strength is...

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:03.700
sumo wrestling.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.250
S-Sumo wrestling?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:11.330
Since sumo wrestling doesn't involve 
any equipment, I think I'd do okay at it.

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:16.050
Why don't we start a Sumo Club together?

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.500
You'd make a good sumo wrestler.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:22.010
<i>P-People do say I have the face and build</i>

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:24.280
<i>of someone who belongs in a Sumo Club, but...</i>

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:30.940
Let's go to Ryogoku together.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:35.630
Come on.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.540
"C-Come on"?

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.010
That was close.

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:44.830
I almost joined your club...

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:46.410
I'm joking.

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:53.050
Sekizan-kun, you should totally play rugby!

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:57.300
Why does it have to be me?

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.680
There are plenty of others out there.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:04.190
You're right that it's better for 
the team to have more members,

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:06.750
since you need fifteen players 
to field a rugby team.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.710
That can't be denied.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:14.860
But, more importantly, I want to show 
you how great rugby is.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.610
"How great rugby is"?

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:22.900
Rugby's a sport you play with your body.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:27.490
A team's strength is built 
on strong guys, agile guys,

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:29.890
and guys who are good at kicking.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:34.870
Each person does what he can in a team sport.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:39.640
It may not be an individual sport,
but it has positions for each kind of player.

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:43.640
Sekizan-kun, there's something 
that only you can do.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.790
Something only... I can do?

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:52.440
It's a sport that finds potential in guys 
who have never played sports before.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:53.500
So...

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:00.500
Please join the rugby team.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:03.630
Please!

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:08.990
If you insist.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.160
Really?!

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:13.120
I'll bring you an 
application form right away.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.550
S-Sure.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:21.740
Wait a minute.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:24.360
Aren't those guys 
your team's upperclassmen?

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:25.930
Huh?

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.240
What are you guys doing?

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:31.450
It's not even dusk yet,
and they're already going home.

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:32.740
Oh, they're just—

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:35.000
They haven't even broken a sweat.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.320
They seem carefree and boisterous.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.660
You're the only passionate one on the team?

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:44.920
Once a promising player like you 
joins the team, I'm <i>sure</i> they'll—

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:46.290
That seems unlikely.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:53.710
If you're just looking for enough players 
to keep the team going, I'm out.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:13:00.630
I'm not going to waste my precious 
three years here on a team like that.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:08.690
I won't give up!

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:13.060
No matter how much I annoy you, 
I won't give up until you say yes!

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.980
Rugby Magazines

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.980
Teehee...

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:20.980
<b>What are these 
doing in my bag?</b>

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:23.990
Teehee...

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:23.990
<b>Hachioji...</b>

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:23.990
<b>Hachioji-kun
 is trouble...</b>

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:28.430
Hachi-senpai, you were pretty persistent.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:30.870
But Captain, you were pretty stubborn, too.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:31.950
You said it.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:35.710
Were you that desperate to lounge 
around in the Going Home Club?

00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:37.330
Who knows...

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:43.540
The way I see it,
Sekizan's like a giant train engine.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.470
A train engine?

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:48.600
It's not that he's apathetic.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:51.850
It just takes more than a little 
fuel to get him moving.

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:55.480
But once he starts moving, 
he can't be stopped.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:57.140
That's the kind of guy he is.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.980
Huh.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.440
Ready...

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:14.330
You're like a train engine.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:17.830
It's a waste for you to be 
part of the Going Home Club.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.710
I don't <i>dislike</i> exercise.

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:23.730
If anything, I actually like working out.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:24.850
Then—

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:27.200
The track and field team 
invited me to join them.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:28.050
What?

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:34.140
In individual events, whether you win 
or lose depends on your own performance.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:33.140
Ready...

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:35.690
It's nice and simple.

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:40.180
Maybe so, but team sports 
offer an excitement and joy

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:43.760
that can't be found in individual sports.

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:45.240
Like I told you before...

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:49.950
It's awesome when you beat a strong opponent 
with your members' individual strengths,

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:55.100
and it makes you glad 
you played rugby with them!

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:56.780
All the more reason, then.

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:57.410
Huh?

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:01.720
At the very least, I'd never choose 
to be on <i>this</i> school's rugby team.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:03.170
But why not?

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:06.670
I hate half-assing things.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.910
The guys on the track and field team said...

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:16.200
that the school's rugby team hasn't even 
won a practice match in the past few years.

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:19.940
Although, I guess that's not surprising, 
considering what I witnessed.

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.220
That's because...

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:30.450
Are you satisfied with doing 
some half-assed exercise?

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:39.670
I'm not half-assing anything!

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:43.920
I don't know much about rugby,

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.940
but as far as I can tell...

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:49.300
from watching our team, it's nothing
 more than a halfhearted game.

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:59.260
Rugby is <i>not</i> a halfhearted sport!

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:02.640
You shouldn't be saying that when 
you've never even played before!

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.750
Don't underestimate rugby!

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:11.790
Jeez, you guys totally got into a fight.

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:13.720
A-And then?

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:16.120
I need to know what happened next.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:22.020
I can't believe things turned 
out the way they did.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:27.190
You're going to tell them about<i> that?</i>

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:35.090
Sekizan-kun

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:50.050
What?

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:03.900
<i>Dear Sekizan-kun...</i>

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:07.820
<i>My heart hasn't stopped 
pounding since I saw you.</i>

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:14.660
<i>You may think a letter is little old-fashioned, 
but I had to tell you how I feel.</i>

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:18.570
<i>I think you'd make a great athlete.</i>

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:22.380
<i>You should play a sport. 
Like rugby, for example.</i>

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:24.790
<i>I'll be cheering for you.</i>

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:25.640
<i>Mutsumi.</i>

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:28.900
"Mutsumi"?

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.400
I'm Hachioji Mutsumi.

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:34.000
It's him!

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:37.610
How was that?

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:39.050
Thanks.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:40.610
Here's your yakisoba roll.

00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:41.920
Yippee!

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:49.940
Hachi-senpai, you're so mean.

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:50.910
Seriously.

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:53.960
How could you tell
the underclassmen that story?!

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:57.970
But you joined the team 
because of it, so who cares?

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:58.840
What?

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:01.500
Don't you remember the bit at the end?

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:02.480
No.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:06.130
I tore it up immediately.

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:08.600
No, I was watching.

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:19.670
<i>By the way, I have a message for 
you from H-kun in our class.</i>

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:21.660
They're both you.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:25.150
<i>The current upperclassmen 
may not be motivated,</i>

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:29.410
<i>but that's why we should change the team,</i>

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:33.090
<i>and create our ideal team
when we're third years.</i>

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:40.540
Really? That's when you finally 
decided to join, Captain?

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:41.310
No.

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:42.080
What?

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:44.970
If anything, that made me 
decide to turn you down.

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:47.060
What? Really?

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.780
Why wouldn't it?

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:51.350
A rugby team is made up of fifteen players.

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:54.120
Having a couple of motivated players 
on the team means nothing.

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:58.720
Sit around waiting for
 the upperclassmen to retire,

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:01.320
and your own retirement will sneak up on you.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:04.440
Sorry, but I didn't have that kind of time.

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:05.670
No way!

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:06.970
Then, when you came to the club room...

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:10.330
Honestly, I went to the 
club room to turn you down.

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:17.090
Is anyone here?

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:19.840
<b>Rugby Team</b>

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:21.800
Excuse me.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:24.800
No one in here, huh?

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:37.940
I need to keep my center of gravity lower.

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:10.880
Hey.

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:11.550
Huh?

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:15.760
Sekizan-kun...

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:18.390
Why are you just standing there?

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:20.590
That was a pass from a genius.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.780
Sorry. I lied.

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:27.430
I know.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:36.040
You told me not to underestimate rugby.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:38.800
Yeah.

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:51.740
Teach me how to play rugby.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:05.840
That's it. Next time, you throw it, 
put some spin on it.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:06.820
Use your wrist.

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:08.840
Like this?

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:10.080
Yeah, that's it.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:12.800
It's flying straighter now, see?

00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:13.750
Yeah.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:15.900
Next, we'll practice catching.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:22.820
<b>Rugby Team</b>

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:19.620
Get under the ball and catch it 
in the middle of your chest.

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:24.210
That's it. Good!

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:25.770
This is pretty fun.

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:26.930
We're just getting started.

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:29.140
This isn't rugby yet.

00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:35.730
What a great story!

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:38.580
I'm fired up now!

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:41.000
Tree Trunk, let's go practice again!

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.800
What? Now?

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:44.540
Hurry up, Tree Trunk!

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:47.930
W-Wait, Gion-kun...

00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:49.510
E-Excuse me!

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:51.740
Don't push yourselves too hard.

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:56.850
We found some nice underclassmen.

00:21:57.660 --> 00:21:58.420
Yeah.

00:21:59.230 --> 00:22:01.180
I'm looking forward to 
our summer training camp.

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:06.880
It'll be...

00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:09.230
...our last summer.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>Next time: "X Day"</b>

00:23:45.870 --> 00:23:48.460
Next time: "X Day."
